# model.zd — a module. Every `.zd` file is one (spec §14D.2).
#
# Nothing here says it is a library and nothing marks a declaration
# exportable: all top-level declarations are importable, and the importing
# file decides what it wants by naming it after `for`.
#
# A module is a unit of *naming*, never of deployment. This file could
# declare `client`, `server` and `durable` state side by side and the
# placement pass would split it as usual — a module with a placement would
# reintroduce exactly the tier-separated file layout the language exists to
# remove.

record Item
    id   is Text
    name is Text

function visible with all
    from all
    take first 20
